# TEST-ONLY TLS identity for the mock OIDC provider (#430). Not a secret. Never used outside tests.

oidc-test-ca.pem        TEST-ONLY CA certificate ("MQLens TEST-ONLY OIDC CA").
oidc-test-idp.crt.pem   TEST-ONLY leaf certificate, SAN DNS:host.docker.internal, signed by the CA above.
oidc-test-idp.key.pem   TEST-ONLY private key for that leaf (PKCS#8, P-256).

Used only by src-tauri/src/oidc/handshake_tests.rs: mongod refuses a plain-HTTP
OIDC issuer, so the mock IdP serves TLS with this leaf, the throwaway Percona
container started by scripts/oidc-percona-fixture.sh trusts this CA, and the
test's own HTTP client trusts it. Nothing else trusts it; never install it
into a real trust store.

The CA's private key was discarded after signing, so no further certificates
can be issued under this CA. Both certificates expire in 2046. To regenerate
(Git Bash needs MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 for the -subj arguments):

  openssl req -x509 -newkey ec -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -nodes \
    -keyout ca.key -out oidc-test-ca.pem -days 7300 \
    -subj "/CN=MQLens TEST-ONLY OIDC CA" \
    -addext "basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE" \
    -addext "keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign"
  openssl req -newkey ec -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -nodes \
    -keyout leaf.key -out leaf.csr -subj "/CN=host.docker.internal"
  printf 'basicConstraints=critical,CA:FALSE\nkeyUsage=critical,digitalSignature\nextendedKeyUsage=serverAuth\nsubjectAltName=DNS:host.docker.internal\n' > leaf.ext
  openssl x509 -req -in leaf.csr -CA oidc-test-ca.pem -CAkey ca.key -CAcreateserial \
    -out oidc-test-idp.crt.pem -days 7300 -extfile leaf.ext
  openssl pkcs8 -topk8 -nocrypt -in leaf.key -out oidc-test-idp.key.pem
  rm ca.key ca.srl leaf.key leaf.csr leaf.ext
